course: dictionary
lesson: 2445
title: Rude words and how to spot them
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Some words are rude, and you will hear them in films, books and from grown-ups when they are cross. The context shows you what a rude word means. «Damn! I missed the bus.» The person is angry or annoyed, because they missed the bus.
explain: Rude words can also make another word stronger. «That was a damn good idea» means the idea was very good, not bad. Read the words around the rude word to find its meaning, just as you would with any other new word.
explain: Knowing a rude word is not the same as using it. You can understand what it means, but at school you should not say it. If you hear one, you can ask a teacher or a grown-up what the sentence means.
fact: «Damn» is a rude word, a mild swear word.
fact: People say «Damn!» when they are angry, annoyed or disappointed.
fact: «Darn» is a mild word used instead of «damn».
fact: «Bother!» is an old-fashioned British mild word for annoyance, used instead of «damn».
fact: «Damning» can mean showing clearly that someone did wrong, as in «damning evidence».
exercise: «Damn! I missed the bus.» What does the word damn show? | Hunger before lunch | Happiness at a party | Tiredness after a long sleep | *Anger or annoyance
exercise: Which word is a mild word people use instead of damn? | Dinner | *Darn | Darkness | Dancer
exercise: Maya thinks «a damn good idea» means a very bad idea. What does it really mean? | A very bad idea | A late idea | An idea about a dog | *A very good idea, because damn makes good stronger
test: In «damning evidence», what does damning mean? | Quiet and calm | *Showing clearly that someone did wrong | Very shiny and bright | Full of birds and song
test: You hear a rude word in a film. What should you do? | Shout it at your friends | *Understand what it means, but do not use it at school | Write it on the board | Repeat it loudly at school
exam: Why should you recognise damn but not use it at school? | Because it means happy | *Because it is a rude word you may hear, but you should not say it at school | Because it is a number | Because it is a French word
